{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"injurious-neutral-glowworm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Severity: the only known defect that makes rebar write WRONG data into Jira\n\nEvery other DC gap found so far causes rebar to read incomplete data or fail loudly. This one silently\ncreates a SECOND Jira issue for the same local ticket — the exact outcome the write-ahead binding\nprotocol exists to prevent.\n\n## The defect (verified in source)\n\n`binding_store.recover_pending`, keyless-pending branch (`binding_store.py:521-531`):\n\n    colon_label = f\"rebar-id:{local_id}\"\n    results = client.search_issues(f'labels = \"{colon_label}\"')\n    if not results:\n        results = client.search_issues(f'labels = \"rebar-id-{local_id}\"')   # legacy form\n    if results:\n        self.bind_confirm(local_id, results[0][\"key\"])\n    else:\n        self.unbind(local_id)\n\nIts own docstring states the inference: *\"Confirm if found; unbind if not (the create never reached\nJira).\"*\n\nThe keyless-pending state is entered PRECISELY when rebar crashed before/during `create_issue` — i.e.\nexactly when the issue may already exist but not yet be acknowledged. Recovery then asks a **JQL\nsearch** whether it exists.\n\n## Why the inference is sound on Cloud and UNSOUND on Data Center\n\nJira DC's Lucene index is explicitly EVENTUALLY CONSISTENT: each cluster node polls for index changes\nroughly once per second, and replication can fall arbitrarily behind. Atlassian's KB\n(\"Lucene index synchronization in Jira Data Center\") and JRASERVER-70423 document real-world lag —\none report of the index being behind by 2,991 seconds (~50 minutes).\n\nA JQL search CANNOT see an issue that is not yet indexed. So on a lagging DC cluster the recovery\nconcludes \"the create never landed\", unbinds, and the NEXT PASS CREATES A DUPLICATE.\n\n## The authors already solved this for the other branch\n\nThe same docstring says of the KEYED-pending branch: *\"NO Jira search — deterministic, so a hard crash\nin the create->label window yields NO duplicate.\"* So the duplicate hazard was understood and\nengineered away where a key was known. The keyless branch falls back to search because there is no\nkey — and search is the index-dependent operation.\n\nRelated, quieter instance of the same hazard: `add_label` writes via REST, but nothing can FIND that\nlabel until the index catches up, so any same-pass label-based dedup is racy on DC.\n\n## Mitigation options, cheapest first\n\n1. **Never unbind on a single negative search.** Require N consecutive misses across passes, or a\n   minimum binding age, before concluding non-existence. Cheapest, and it converts a silent duplicate\n   into a delayed correct answer.\n2. **Prefer a non-indexed confirmation.** A direct GET on a recorded key already covers the keyed\n   branch; the gap is only keyless, where by definition no key exists — so consider recording the key\n   earlier, or narrowing the window.\n3. **At minimum, on the DC backend: log loudly and LEAVE THE BINDING PENDING rather than unbinding.**\n   A stuck pending binding is recoverable; a duplicate Jira issue is not.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] a test simulates DC index lag (a search returning empty for an issue that DOES exist) and\n      asserts recover_pending does NOT unbind — today it does, and the next pass duplicates\n- [ ] the chosen mitigation is applied to the keyless-pending branch, and the keyed branch's\n      no-search determinism is UNCHANGED (it is already correct)\n- [ ] the behaviour difference between Cloud and DC is documented at the call site, with the reason\n      (eventual-consistency of the DC Lucene index), so the next reader does not 'simplify' it back\n- [ ] [operator-attested] the mitigation is exercised against the live DC harness","id":"21fc-51d7-90ca-4a03","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"DC index lag makes recover_pending unbind a live create, producing DUPLICATE Jira issues"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785496946839101001,"uuid":"be1f7853-45ca-41c9-8b03-7d4f33e4cf90"}